ears it. A promise rejection that still has no handler once pending promise callbacks have run counts as an uncaught error, so a `fetch` chain without a `catch` fails the Deck App instead of failing silently.\n _Avoid_: Crash screen, red box, blank screen\n \n **Runtime Upload Archive**:\n","complete":true,"hunks":[{"path":"CONTEXT.md","oldStart":169,"oldLines":7,"newStart":169,"newLines":7,"header":"@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ Restarting the Deck App JavaScript runtime with a fresh context after **Runtime","language":"markdown","lines":[{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":169,"newNumber":169,"text":"_Avoid_: Hot reload, refresh, soft reload"},{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":170,"newNumber":170,"text":""},{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":171,"newNumber":171,"text":"**Deck App Failure Screen**:"},{"kind":"del","oldNumber":172,"newNumber":null,"text":"The VitaDeck-painted screen that replaces the **Active Deck App** after it throws an uncaught error (during boot, render, effects, input handlers, or timers), showing the error message, the first lines of its stack, and that **Start Input** opens the **VitaDeck Shell**. A **Deck App Runtime Restart** clears it."},{"kind":"add","oldNumber":null,"newNumber":172,"text":"The VitaDeck-painted screen that replaces the **Active Deck App** after it throws an uncaught error (during boot, render, effects, input handlers, or timers), showing the error message, the first lines of its stack, and that **Start Input** opens the **VitaDeck Shell**. A **Deck App Runtime Restart** clears it. A promise rejection that still has no handler once pending promise callbacks have run counts as an uncaught error, so a `fetch` chain without a `catch` fails the Deck App instead of failing silently."},{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":173,"newNumber":173,"text":"_Avoid_: Crash screen, red box, blank screen"},{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":174,"newNumber":174,"text":""},{"kind":"ctx","oldNumber":175,"newNumber":175,"text":"**Runtime Upload Archive**:"}]}]}]}
